{"qid":"Q370736","names":["British Cape Colony"],"title":"British Cape Colony","endonym":{"native":"Cape Colony","lang":"en"},"capsule":"The Cape Colony was a British colonial possession at the southern tip of Africa, first seized from the Batavian Republic in 1795 to deny the Cape sea route to France, returned in 1803, and retaken after the Battle of Blaauwberg in 1806, with British sovereignty formally confirmed in 1814. Under British rule the colony expanded dramatically eastward through the Cape Frontier Wars against Xhosa kingdoms and northward as Boer settlers (Voortrekkers) departed in the Great Trek of 1836–40; the abolition of slavery in 1834 was a principal Boer grievance. Representative government was granted in 1853 and responsible government in 1872; the colony's boundaries grew further after diamonds were discovered near Hopetown on the Orange River in 1867 and at Kimberley in 1871, and it was incorporated into the Union of South Africa in 1910.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Cape Colony territorial extent is well documented by British colonial surveys and maps from the early 19th century onward; pre-1820 northern and eastern boundaries were less formally defined and expanded through successive military campaigns, so the dataset geometry for the early period is broadly approximated.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Cape Colony","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape_Colony"},{"label":"Britannica: Cape Colony","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Cape-Colony"}],"britannica":"place/Cape-Colony","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Cape Colony","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Georg